# Home Assistant Community App: UniFi OS Server

[![Release][release-shield]][release] ![Project Stage][project-stage-shield] ![Project Maintenance][maintenance-shield]

[![Sponsor Frenck via GitHub Sponsors][github-sponsors-shield]][github-sponsors]

[![Support Frenck on Patreon][patreon-shield]][patreon]

UniFi OS Server lets you manage your UniFi network using a web browser,
right from Home Assistant.

## Important notice

**This version replaces the UniFi Network Application with UniFi OS Server.**
The update cannot be undone without restoring a Home Assistant backup of this
app made before the update.

- Make a Home Assistant backup of this app before updating.
- If you use a local UniFi account (not a Ubiquiti account), export a `.unf`
  backup from the current UniFi Network Application before updating.
- Plan for at least 4 GB of RAM (8 GB preferred) and 25 GB of free disk
  space.
- Home Assistant does not install this update automatically.

Read the app documentation before updating.

## About

This app runs Ubiquiti's UniFi OS Server, including the UniFi Network
application, on your Home Assistant system. It installs UniFi OS Server with
Ubiquiti's official, unmodified installer, and the web interface opens inside
Home Assistant.

When you update from the UniFi Network Application, the first start upgrades
your existing UniFi data and installs UniFi OS Server. Ubiquiti's setup wizard
then imports your Network configuration.

This app supports 64-bit systems (`aarch64` and `amd64`).

